<section class="section section--tint" id="who" aria-labelledby="who-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Before you hire anyone</p>
      <h2 id="who-title">Which professional does your work need?</h2>
      <p>"Accountant" is used loosely. Some work is routine, and some the law limits to named professionals. Check which yours is before you engage someone.</p>
    </header>

    <table class="who-table" aria-labelledby="who-title">
      <thead><tr class="who-table__row who-table__row--head">
        <th scope="col">The work</th>
        <th scope="col">Who usually handles it</th>
        <th scope="col">What to keep in mind</th>
      </tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr class="who-table__row">
        <th scope="row"><strong>Bookkeeping, ledgers, bank reconciliation</strong></th>
        <td class="who-table__who">Accountant or bookkeeper</td>
        <td>Ask about experience with your kind of business and your software.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="who-table__row">
        <th scope="row"><strong>Preparing and filing GST returns</strong></th>
        <td class="who-table__who">Accountant, GST practitioner or CA</td>
        <td>Responsibility for what a practitioner files stays with you, the registered person. Review before you confirm.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="who-table__row">
        <th scope="row"><strong>Appearing for you on a GST matter</strong></th>
        <td class="who-table__who">An authorised representative</td>
        <td>The law lists who qualifies, including advocates; practising CAs, cost accountants and company secretaries; and GST practitioners you have authorised. Ask which category applies.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="who-table__row">
        <th scope="row"><strong>Preparing an income tax return</strong></th>
        <td class="who-table__who">Accountant, tax practitioner or CA</td>
        <td>The return is yours. Read it before it is verified, and keep the records behind it.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="who-table__row">
        <th scope="row"><strong>Appearing for you on an income tax matter</strong></th>
        <td class="who-table__who">An authorised representative</td>
        <td>Authorised by you in writing, and within the categories the Act lists, such as a legal practitioner or a practising CA.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="who-table__row">
        <th scope="row"><strong>Statutory audit of a company</strong></th>
        <td class="who-table__who">Chartered Accountant only</td>
        <td>Others can help prepare schedules and reconciliations. That is audit support, and it is not an audit.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="who-table__row">
        <th scope="row"><strong>Udyam registration</strong></th>
        <td class="who-table__who">You can do it yourself</td>
        <td>The <a href="https://udyamregistration.gov.in/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">official portal<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> states that registration is free. Any fee you pay elsewhere is for optional help.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody></table>

    <div class="who-notes">
      <div class="asklist">
        <h3>Five questions to ask before you engage anyone</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Which membership or enrolment do you hold, and what is the number?</li>
          <li>Who will actually do my work?</li>
          <li>What is included, what is not, and what is the total fee in writing, with GST and government charges shown?</li>
          <li>Who will have access to my portals and data, and how do I withdraw it?</li>
          <li>If we part ways, how do I get my books and records back?</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="callout">
        <h3>If your work needs a Chartered Accountant</h3>
        <p>Work reserved for CAs needs a CA. ICAI runs its own search for practising CAs and CA firms, called <a href="https://caconnect.icai.org/search-your-ca" rel="noopener" target="_blank">CA Connect<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. You do not need AccountOrbit to use it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="who-source">General information drawn from the CGST Act, 2017 (sections 48 and 116), the Income-tax Act, 2025 (section 515) and the Companies Act, 2013 (section 141). Checked November 2026. This is general information and has not been reviewed by a qualified professional. Rules change, so confirm the position for your own case.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
