      <p>AccountOrbit makes the introduction. It does not become a party to the work.</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>You describe the work</h3>
        <p>Tell us what you need done and a little about your business.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>We review the requirement</h3>
        <p>We look at what kind of professional the work calls for, including whether it is reserved for a particular qualification.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>An introduction, where possible</h3>
        <p>If a suitable professional is available and you have agreed to your details being shared, we introduce you. If not, no introduction is made.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>You decide, and deal directly</h3>
        <p>Check their credentials, and engage them only if you are satisfied. The engagement is between you and them.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="about__intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--gold">About AccountOrbit</p>
        <h2 id="about-title">A referral platform that shows its working</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about__text">
        <p>Looking for an accountant in Delhi usually means sorting through firms, directories and online filing services. It is rarely clear who will do the work, what they are qualified to do, or what happens to your phone number after you submit it.</p>
        <p>AccountOrbit, owned by {{ site.owner.name }}, helps individuals and businesses in Delhi work out what kind of help they need and enquire about a suitable professional. The work, and the responsibility for it, stays with the professional you choose.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--gold about__cta" href="/request-an-accountant/">Find an Accountant</a>
        <p class="about__more">More on <a href="/about-us/">who runs AccountOrbit</a> and <a href="/how-it-works/">how it works</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="about__sub">What you can hold us to</h3>
    <ul class="trust-grid">
      <li class="trust-card">
        <h4>An introduction, not a firm</h4>
        <p>We take enquiries and make introductions. We are not a CA firm, law firm, audit practice, tax authority or government service.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="trust-card">
        <h4>The professional does the work</h4>
        <p>Advice, filings and professional responsibility sit with the person you engage. We do not set their fees, so ask for yours in writing.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="trust-card">
        <h4>Evidence, not claims</h4>
        <p>We show no client counts, ratings, awards or testimonials, because we have none verified to show. Check any professional's credentials at the source.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="about__columns">
      <div id="questions" class="questions">
        <h3 class="about__sub">Questions people ask first</h3>
        <details>
          <summary>Is AccountOrbit a CA firm? Will you file my returns?</summary>
          <p>No to both. AccountOrbit is an independent referral platform. It does not employ accountants or perform accounting, audit, tax or legal work. Any filing is done by the professional you engage, and your responsibilities as the taxpayer continue.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What does this cost?</summary>
          <p>Fees for professional work are agreed between you and the professional, and AccountOrbit does not set them. {% pending "whether enquiries are free, and how AccountOrbit earns money." %}</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Who will see my details?</summary>
          <p>Your details are used to review your enquiry, and are shared with a professional being considered for your work only if you have agreed. A privacy policy will set this out in full before the site goes live.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Will I definitely be matched?</summary>
          <p>No. An introduction depends on a suitable professional being available for your work and your area. We will not describe someone as suitable just to close an enquiry. {% pending "how and when visitors are told when no introduction can be made." %}</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do you have an office in my area?</summary>
          <p>Please do not assume so. Naming a Delhi area on this site does not mean AccountOrbit or a professional has an office there. Ask any professional where they work from and whether they can visit.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Who runs AccountOrbit?</summary>
          <p>AccountOrbit is owned by {{ site.owner.name }}. You can find {{ site.owner.name }} on <a href="{{ site.owner.facebook }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Facebook<span class="visually-hidden"> (personal profile, opens in a new tab)</span></a> and <a href="{{ site.owner.instagram }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Instagram<span class="visually-hidden"> (personal profile, opens in a new tab)</span></a>. These are personal profiles, not AccountOrbit company pages. {% pending "the operating entity behind AccountOrbit." %}</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do you list accounting jobs?</summary>
          <p>No. AccountOrbit is for people looking for accounting help, not for job seekers.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <section id="delhi" aria-labelledby="delhi-title">
        <h3 class="about__sub" id="delhi-title">Delhi, by how businesses work</h3>
        <p class="delhi-intro">We accept enquiries from across Delhi. These groups show how local accounting needs differ. They are not a list of offices or a promise that a professional is available in a given area.</p>
        <ul class="delhi-list">
